# LedgerSG — Root Environment Index
#
# No process reads variables from the repository root: the two applications
# each load their own env file —
#
#   apps/backend/.env   (Django/DRF API — read by config/settings/*.py)
#   apps/web/.env.local (Next.js frontend — read by next.config.ts, middleware,
#                       src/lib/api-client.ts, src/lib/server/api-client.ts)
#
# Start each app from its verified template (do not edit this index into a
# real env — it contains no values, only the map):
#
#   cp apps/backend/.env.example apps/backend/.env
#   cp apps/web/.env.example    apps/web/.env.local
#
# Combined variable set (every live variable, verified against the code —
# backend per docs/REMEDIATION_PLAN_2026-11-21_P3.md D-4, web per
# docs/REMEDIATION_PLAN_2026-11-21_P2.md B-4):
#
# ── apps/backend/.env ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#   DEBUG                  Django debug mode (never true in production)
#   SECRET_KEY             Django secret — generate a real value in production
#   DJANGO_SETTINGS_MODULE config.settings.development | production
#   ALLOWED_HOSTS          comma-separated hostnames the API serves
#   DB_NAME                PostgreSQL database name (e.g. ledgersg_dev)
#   DB_USER                PostgreSQL role
#   DB_PASSWORD            PostgreSQL role password
#   DB_HOST                PostgreSQL host (127.0.0.1 locally)
#   DB_PORT                PostgreSQL port (5432)
#   REDIS_URL              Redis — Celery broker AND the Django cache backing
#                          the org-membership cache and rate limiting (SEC-002)
#   CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS   comma-separated browser origins (the web app URLs)
#   RATELIMIT_ENABLE       auth rate limits on/off (testing.py forces off)
#   DEBUG_TOOLBAR          django-debug-toolbar (development settings only)
#   CELERY_ALWAYS_EAGER    run Celery tasks inline (development only)
#   SENTRY_DSN             optional error-reporting DSN
#   ADMIN_EMAIL            health-check/admin recipient
#
# ── apps/web/.env.local ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL    browser-facing API URL (http://localhost:8000 dev)
#   BACKEND_URL            server-side (SSR/server-action) API URL
#   NEXT_OUTPUT_MODE       "export" (static CDN) | "standalone" (server)
#
# Reserved-but-unread frontend flags stay documented in
# apps/web/.env.example until the features that read them ship.
#
# The P4 session-persistence cookies need NO environment variables: the
# HttpOnly refresh cookie and the session_hint marker are set/cleared by the
# auth endpoints themselves (see apps/backend/apps/core/views/_refresh_cookie.py
# and docs/DEPLOYMENT.md §9 for the cross-site SameSite caveat).
